IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`

-- Tests for Regulations s 1 (definitions). Expected values are decided from the text
-- of s 1: "payment period" (July 1 to June 30), "release", "applicant", "beneficiary".

§ `Regulations s 1 -- tests`

-- "applicant": applied, or an application was made on their behalf.
#ASSERT `the person is an applicant` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the person is an applicant` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is an applicant` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an applicant` FALSE FALSE)

-- "beneficiary": payment approved, or a benefit became payable on their behalf.
#ASSERT `the person is a beneficiary` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the person is a beneficiary` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a beneficiary` FALSE FALSE)

-- "payment period": 1 July to 30 June. The last day of June belongs to the period
-- that began the July before; the first day of July starts a new one.
#ASSERT `the payment period that includes the day` (YMD 2025 6 30) EQUALS `Payment period` WITH `the first day of the payment period` IS YMD 2024 7 1, `the last day of the payment period` IS YMD 2025 6 30
#ASSERT `the payment period that includes the day` (YMD 2025 7 1) EQUALS `Payment period` WITH `the first day of the payment period` IS YMD 2025 7 1, `the last day of the payment period` IS YMD 2026 6 30
#ASSERT `the payment period that includes the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `Payment period` WITH `the first day of the payment period` IS YMD 2025 7 1, `the last day of the payment period` IS YMD 2026 6 30
#ASSERT `the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` (YMD 2025 6 30) EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT `the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` (YMD 2025 7 1) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS 2025

-- The calendar year taken to be the last taxation year that ended before the period
-- began (fork F8): June 2026 is in the period that began 1 July 2025, so 2024;
-- July 2026 starts the period that began 1 July 2026, so 2025.
#ASSERT `the calendar year taken to be the last taxation year that ended before the payment period that includes the day began` (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT `the calendar year taken to be the last taxation year that ended before the payment period that includes the day began` (YMD 2026 7 15) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the calendar year taken to be the last taxation year that ended before the payment period that includes the day began` (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS 2023

-- "release": earned remission and the expiry of a sentence always count; a parole or
-- a statutory release counts only if it has not been terminated or revoked.
`a release on earned remission` MEANS `Release event` WITH
    `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
    `the way of the release` IS `release on earned remission`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE

`a release at the expiry of the sentence` MEANS `Release event` WITH
    `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
    `the way of the release` IS `release at the expiry of the sentence`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE

`a parole that stands` MEANS `Release event` WITH
    `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
    `the way of the release` IS `release on parole`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE

`a parole that was revoked` MEANS `Release event` WITH
    `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
    `the way of the release` IS `release on parole`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS TRUE

`a statutory release that stands` MEANS `Release event` WITH
    `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
    `the way of the release` IS `release on statutory release`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE

`a statutory release that was terminated` MEANS `Release event` WITH
    `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
    `the way of the release` IS `release on statutory release`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the event is a release` `a release on earned remission`
#ASSERT `the event is a release` `a release at the expiry of the sentence`
#ASSERT `the event is a release` `a parole that stands`
#ASSERT NOT (`the event is a release` `a parole that was revoked`)
#ASSERT `the event is a release` `a statutory release that stands`
#ASSERT NOT (`the event is a release` `a statutory release that was terminated`)
